# Round 59: pins the for-body exemption's REMAINING half. tmp is ASSIGNED
# in the body, so it is loop-local (the VM's for-scope rule) and reads of
# it inside the body are not module-scope uses -- the order guard must not
# count them against the later module binding `tmp is 99`. This is the
# false-refusal case the round-58 skip was protecting; round 59 narrowed
# the skip to exactly this axis (binder + body-assigned names) after the
# blanket version hid genuine reads.
for i in range of 2:
    tmp is i
    print of tmp
tmp is 99
print of tmp
